{"id":"chatcmpl-d3dde258-c56e-4b20-b1b4-33a3a0bd9071","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244531,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"{\n  \"highlights\": \"When visual question answering tools disagree on a medical image finding, the successful strategy was to query multiple independent vision-language models and rely on positive consensus among those that provided specific, consistent descriptions. The approach prioritized resolving conflicts through additional evidence rather than accepting a single negative or ambiguous result.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When initial tool outputs conflict, query additional independent tools to build a consensus rather than defaulting to the first or most authoritative-sounding response.\",\n    \"Weight positive findings with specific descriptive details (location, trajectory) more heavily than negative or non-informative outputs when determining laterality.\",\n    \"Use a verification step to explicitly flag conflicts and trigger further evidence gathering before finalizing an answer.\",\n    \"When image orientation (e.g., lateral view) limits direct laterality assessment, infer side from trajectory and position descriptions provided by multiple models.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical Imaging QA\": \"Query at least two independent vision-language models; if they disagree, add more models until a clear positive consensus emerges; prefer specific positive descriptions over vague negatives.\",\n    \"Conflict Resolution\": \"Treat tool disagreement as a signal to gather more evidence, not as a tie to be broken arbitrarily; use a verification tool to document the conflict and justify additional queries.\",\n    \"Laterality Determination\": \"On lateral views, rely on trajectory and anterior-posterior position cues described by models to infer right vs left; cross-validate across multiple models.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm that at least two independent tools positively identify the finding with consistent laterality before finalizing.\",\n    \"Ensure any conflicting or negative tool outputs are explicitly noted and resolved through additional evidence, not ignored.\"\n  ]\n}"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":734,"total_tokens":1087,"completion_tokens":353,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":734},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":353}}}